== 1. the log law (4.2): exact at a doubling, bounded error between, monotone, no overflow
   Base 100000, DoublingBP 200: gain at X = Base * (2^k - 1) must be exactly k * DoublingBP
   exact at 21 doublings: True
   largest |true - integer| over 200 000 random X: 16.65 bp of gain = 0.083 of one doubling (the interpolation bound is 0.086)
   monotone in X on a grid: True
   at X = 2^50, Base 1, DoublingBP 10 000 (the bounds): gain 500000, the product 2048000000 is far below 2^63 = 9223372036854775808
   the years to each doubling for 1 000 households, one execution each, every tick (placeholder):
   1: 0.3y  2: 0.8y  3: 1.9y  4: 4.1y  5: 8.5y  6: 17.3y  7: 34.8y  8: 69.9y

== 2. the trend (4.3): carried remainder, exact over any whole number of years
   TrendBP     1: after 3 years      3 (exact      3), carry 0
   TrendBP   137: after 3 years    411 (exact    411), carry 0
   TrendBP   200: after 3 years    600 (exact    600), carry 0
   TrendBP  9999: after 3 years  29997 (exact  29997), carry 0

== 3. discovery (4.4): the keyed hash hits at the stated rate and takes no word per tick
   60 active cells over 200 years (4380000 cell-ticks)
   DiscoveryBP  expected  observed
            50      60.0        72
           500     600.0       618
          5000    6000.0      6071
         10000   12000.0     11962
   two keys, one cell, DiscoveryBP 5 000: hits 31 and 27, hit on both 0 (independent: about 0.0)
   one key, cells 0 and 1: hit on both 0 of 31 and 31

== 4. diffusion (4.5): a lagging cell approaches w * frontier from below, never passes it; no order effect
   Reach 100; frontier cell 0 at gain 3000; distances 0-1 20, 0-2 60, 1-2 50; CatchUpBP 2 000 (20% of the gap a year)
   w(20) = 8000, w(60) = 4000, w(50) = 5000; targets: cell 1 -> 2400, cell 2 -> max(1200, cell 1 * w(50))
   year  1: gains [3000, 435, 217]
   year  5: gains [3000, 1517, 758]
   year 10: gains [3000, 2075, 1038]
   year 20: gains [3000, 2356, 1178]
   limits: cell 1 2400; cell 2 the larger of the direct 1200 and the relay through cell 1 (2400 * w(50) = 1200); a relay is a frontier like any, one tick behind, and can pass the direct limit by the product of the two losses (spec 4.5.5: bounded by the product of the weights of the legs, not by w of the total distance)
   the added advance does not depend on the order of the cells (6 permutations): True
   edge 0-1 closed (no path 0 to 1, 1 to 0): the step adds [0, 0, 0] and the carries are [0, 0, 2400000]: cell 1 has no contact and its carry stays 0, cell 2 (60 from cell 0) carries 1 200 * 2 000 = 2 400 000 of 3 650 000 toward its first unit

== 5. the identity of the event (4.6.3): After = Before + Doing + Trend + Discovery + CatchUp - Clamped, Clamped >= 0
   100 000 random cells: Clamped >= 0 and After >= Before in every case: True (smallest Clamped 0)
